      "devanagari": "बाढमित्येव काकुत्स्थ प्रहृष्टेनान्तरात्मना |\nदिव्यभास्वरदेहाश्च मूर्तिमन्तः सुखप्रदाः\nकेचिदङ्गारसदृशाः केचिद् धूमोपमास्तथा |\nचन्द्रार्कसदृशाः केचित् प्रह्वांजलिपुटास्तथा\nरामं प्रांजलयो भूत्वाऽब्रुवन् मधुरभाषिणः |\nइमे स्म नरशार्दूल शाधि किं करवाम ते",
      "iast": "bāḍham iti eva kākutstha prahṛṣṭena antarātmanā |\ndivya bhāsvara dehāḥ ca mūrtimantaḥ sukhapradāḥ\nkecid aṅgāra sadṛśāḥ kecid dhūma upamāḥ tathā |\ncandra arka sadṛśāḥ kecit prahva añjali puṭāḥ tathā\nrāmam prāñjalayo bhūtvā abruvan madhura bhāṣiṇaḥ |\nime sma naraśārdūla śādhi kim karavāma te",
      "translation": "Gladdening in his heart of hearts Rama of Kakutstha received the annulment missiles saying, \"Agreed! Sire!\" Those missiles are with radiantly divine bodies, appealing and endowing bliss. Some are fire-like, some smoke-like, and some moon-like and some sun-like, and such as they are, some of them holding out their hollowed palms, and some with palms adjoined melodiously spoke to Rama saying, \"here we are, oh, manly-tiger, what can we do for you.\"",
